    {
     "author": {
      "accountId": "557058:19472d6c-63f5-479e-9de0-57b80681cff8",
      "accountType": "atlassian",
      "active": true,
      "avatarUrls": {
       "16x16": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/91ba3ae46b5ff6357fbe55622c5d3f9a?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FDD-4.png",
       "24x24": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/91ba3ae46b5ff6357fbe55622c5d3f9a?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FDD-4.png",
       "32x32": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/91ba3ae46b5ff6357fbe55622c5d3f9a?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FDD-4.png",
       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/91ba3ae46b5ff6357fbe55622c5d3f9a?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FDD-4.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Daniel Davis",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=557058%3A19472d6c-63f5-479e-9de0-57b80681cff8",
      "timeZone": "America/New_York"
     },
     "body": "<p><span class=\"error\">&#91;Followup from Sourceforge Tracker&#93;</span><br/>\nFollowup Submitter: fcswa<br/>\nLogged In: YES <br/>\nuser_id=1855086<br/>\nOriginator: NO</p>\n\n<p>According to</p>\n\n<p><a href=\"http://java.sun.com/j2ee/tutorial/1_3-fcs/doc/Servlets12.html\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://java.sun.com/j2ee/tutorial/1_3-fcs/doc/Servlets12.html</a></p>\n\n<p>...this is not a good assumption.  It can cause a long-running (over 2 seconds<br/>\nin Tomcat, by default) API-M request to be abnormally terminated if shutdown is<br/>\noccurring at the same time.</p>\n\n\n<p>------- Additional Comment #1 From Chris Wilper 2006-05-12 13:24 <span class=\"error\">&#91;reply&#93;</span> -------</p>\n\n<p>Workaround:</p>\n\n<p>1) Disallow new API-M requests.<br/>\n2) Wait for any existing requests to complete.<br/>\n3) Stop the server.</p>\n\n<p>For #1, this strategy should work:</p>\n\n<p>You can stop any new requests from getting through to Fedora by putting a policy<br/>\nin play (at runtime) that temporarily restricts access to API-M and API-A.</p>\n\n<p>The following policy can be used as a starting point:<br/>\n<a href=\"http://www.fedora.info/download/2.1.1/userdocs/server/security/xacml-policies/default/repository-wide/deny-apim-if-not-localhost.xml\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://www.fedora.info/download/2.1.1/userdocs/server/security/xacml-policies/default/repository-wide/deny-apim-if-not-localhost.xml</a></p>\n\n<p>After putting it in the correct place, use the fedora-reload-policies tool to<br/>\nput it into play without stopping the server:<br/>\n<a href=\"http://www.fedora.info/download/2.1.1/userdocs/server/cmd-line/index.html#reload\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://www.fedora.info/download/2.1.1/userdocs/server/cmd-line/index.html#reload</a></p>\n\n<p>NOTE: Be sure to remove the \"disallow API-M\" policy before restarting the server<br/>\nagain.</p>\n\n<p>Bug List: (11 of 17) First Last Prev Next   Show list      Search page      Enter new bug</p>",
