  "description": "<p>Fedora's webapp  shutdown currently relies on servlet container to ensure all requests are complete.  However, the servlet container doesn't always wait until requests are finished in order to call destroy().  For long-running requests, this can be problematic because the resources (the db, etc) might be closed before the requests have a chance to finish.</p>",
